WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.200
Text on an ivory background, read aloud: "Rent shouldn't need a screenshot."

00:03.200 --> 00:06.133
Tenant101 on a phone with demo data. The tenant's home shows Unit 101 with ₱81,675 owed, and the tenant taps Pay this rental. "With Tenant101, every tenant sees what they owe, right on their phone."

00:06.133 --> 00:09.900
The pay screen offers GCash, Maya and Card, marked "Confirmed automatically, no receipt to upload and nothing for your landlord to approve by hand." The tenant taps GCash.

00:09.900 --> 00:14.333
PayMongo's checkout, in test mode, shows ₱81,675.00 for Sunrise Apartments 101. The tenant chooses GCash and taps Continue. "They pay with GCash, Maya, or a card, through PayMongo."

00:14.333 --> 00:18.500
Sped up three times, the tenant types their name and email and taps Pay ₱81,675.00.

00:18.500 --> 00:21.867
PayMongo's GCash test payment page. The tenant taps Authorize Test Payment. "A few taps, and the payment goes through."

00:21.867 --> 00:25.233
PayMongo shows "GCash Payment Received!" and the tenant taps Return to Merchant.

00:25.233 --> 00:29.200
Back in Tenant101, Unit 101 reads Paid up, balance ₱0.00. "Back in the app, it's already paid."

00:29.200 --> 00:34.133
Recent payments lists ₱81,675.00 on 26 September 2026, recorded on its own. "No receipt to upload. Nobody approving it by hand."

00:34.133 --> 00:38.133
The lion mark. "Tenant101. Who's paid, and what's next." See how it works at tommydeleon.com. Team project, not launched, demo data.
